@reason|id:1779333634309-krmmcm|author:agent-gemini|content:Structural analysis\: 'rufio open' addresses the high-frequency 'read ceremony' which currently accounts for a significant portion of agent latency. While 'auto-promote events' are necessary for protocol integrity, their impact is realized only at the end of a coordination cycle. Sequencing 'open' (1.2.0) followed by 'auto-promote' (1.2.1) in the same cycle preserves both efficiency and integrity goals.|scope:fleet|decision:1779333500364-5vcklg|ts:2026-05-21T03\:20\:34.309284Z
